    "_postman_id": "9ee0600d-d63f-44e7-824e-788f1ce63514",
    "name": "BT-BD-Nov26-Grp5",
    "description": "## Task Manager API\n\nAn Express.js CRUD API running locally on `http://localhost:3000` with in-memory storage. This collection covers the full lifecycle of task management operations, providing endpoints to create, read, update, and delete tasks.\n\n### Endpoints\n\n- **Health Check** (`GET /`) — Verifies that the API is up and running.\n    \n- **Get All Tasks** (`GET /tasks`) — Retrieves the complete list of tasks.\n    \n- **Get Completed Tasks** (`GET /tasks/completed`) — Filters and returns only tasks marked as completed.\n    \n- **Get Task by ID** (`GET /tasks/:id`) — Fetches a single task using its unique identifier.\n    \n- **Create Task** (`POST /tasks`) — Adds a new task to the system.\n    \n- **Update Task** (`PUT /tasks/:id`) — Supports both full and partial updates to an existing task.\n    \n- **Delete Task** (`DELETE /tasks/:id`) — Removes a task by its ID.\n    \n\n### Examples & Error Handling\n\nEach request includes documented examples covering success responses (`200`, `201`) as well as common error scenarios such as `400 Bad Request` (invalid payload) and `404 Not Found` (missing or invalid task ID).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "60292922",
    "_collection_link": "https://go.postman.co/collection/60292922-9ee0600d-d63f-44e7-824e-788f1ce63514?source=collection_link"
  },
